 "▼ Dive in: <0>Mask on/off</0>": "",
 "A decoder-only LLM may only use tokens <0>at or before</0> the current position.": "",
 "The mask adds −∞ to every score above the diagonal, so softmax gives those positions weight {#}.": "",
 "This lets training check <0>all positions in parallel</0> while each one still only sees its past.": "",
 "Without the mask, position i could just copy token i+{#} — the very answer it is trained to predict.": "",
 "At inference only the newest token's row is computed; earlier K,V are reused from the <0>KV cache</0>.": "",
 "Implementations often add a large negative number instead of true −∞; the effect is the same.": "",
